==Scots==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|sco|ang|dīġan||to die}}, from {{inh|sco|gem-pro|*dawjaną||to die}}. Compare {{cog|en|die}}, {{cog|da|dø}}, {{cog|nn|døy}}, {{cog|nb|dø}}, {{cog|is|deyja}}, {{cog|sv|dö}}, {{cog|fo|doyggja}}.

====Verb====
{{sco-verb|dees|deein|dee'd|dee'd}}

# to [[die]]
#* {{quote-song|1852-1859|William Douglas of Fingland|Annie Laurie|Scottish Songs|http://ks.petruccimusiclibrary.org/files/imglnks/usimg/4/4a/IMSLP275292-PMLP447045-Scottish_Songs.pdf|author=Lady John Scott|/ Maxwelton braes are bonnie, / Where early fa's the dew, / And its there that Annie Laurie, / Gie'd me her promise true / Gie'd me her promise true, / Which ne'er forgot shall be, / And for bonnie Annie Laurie / I'd lay me doon and '''dee'''.}}

===Etymology 2===
Alteration of {{l|sco|dae}}.

====Verb====
{{sco-verb|dees|deein|dee'd|dee'd}}

